            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous plaque rupture and thrombus formation in the left main coronary artery documented by intravascular ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case documents the finding of a spontaneous plaque rupture with thrombus formation in the left main coronary artery of a patient who presented with an infarction of the circumflex artery. This serendipitous observation supports the hypothesis that spontaneous plaque ruptures occur sporadically and do not necessarily lead to occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
